## 4. Test Plan

### New Tests Required

| Test File | Test Name | Description |
|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| `src/table.test.ts` | `renders multi-row table with correct separator` | 3+ flights; verify header row, separator row (each segment length = column width), data rows present |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `right-aligns Price column` | Price values have leading spaces to fill column width; other columns have trailing spaces |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `renders single-row table` | 1 flight; verify header + separator + 1 data row |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `returns "No flights found." for empty array` | `renderTable([])` returns exact string `No flights found.` |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `uses £ as fallback currency` | No `currency` arg → prices prefixed with `£` |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `uses provided currency symbol` | Pass `currency="$"` → prices prefixed with `$` |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `falls back to £ when currency is empty string` | `currency=""` → `£` used |
| `src/table.test.ts` | `column widths are max of header and data` | Verify each column width = `max(header.length, longest data value length)` |
| `src/cli.test.ts` | `calls renderTable and prints to stdout on success` | Mock `searchFlights` to return flights; verify stdout contains table output |
| `src/cli.test.ts` | `writes error to stderr and exits 1 on searchFlights rejection` | Mock `searchFlights` to reject; verify stderr has error message, exit code 1, stdout is empty |

### Regression Scope
- **`src/skyscanner/client.test.ts`** — must still pass (no changes to client.ts)
- **`tsc --noEmit`** — must still pass with zero errors after adding `table.ts` and `table.test.ts`
- **Existing `cli.ts` behavior** — argument parsing, env-var guard, date/adults validation must remain unchanged; only the table rendering portion is refactored

